## Treat Explorer live graph as no simulation for SWRL
================================================================================

Context: Triggering a class SWRL business rule from Knowledge Graph →
Explorer failed with ``Simulation 'live' was not found``. The Explorer
source picker uses ``live`` / ``live:inferred`` as option values; the
rule request posted those tokens as ``simulation_id``, and the API looked
them up in the simulation registry.

Changes:

1. src/front/static/query/js/query-business-rules.js
   Resolve the sandbox id through KgGraphSource so live picker tokens are
   omitted from the request body.
2. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/TwinGraphAccess.py
   Map ``live`` / ``live:inferred`` to no sandbox for every graph source
   payload.
3. src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py
   Skip sandbox lookup when the business-rule request carries a live token.
4. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/node/NodeBusinessRuleService.py
   Run against the live graph when the caller sends a live source token.
5. tests/units/api/test_dtwin_nodes_business_rule.py
   Cover live source tokens on the request route.

